{#- One candidate as a `decide()` item's context (`reconcile.build_items`):
    `user.j2`'s preamble limited to this item -- the campaign date and the
    chronicle lines it shows -- then a heading naming what is asked, then the
    candidate's record and signal block from `user.j2` byte for byte.
    `user.j2` is the legacy one-call prompt's and stays until the switch
    retires it. Vars: now (the campaign date, friendly form, or blank),
    chronicle [{id, one_line}] (only the lines of the scenes this item shows,
    `reconcile.item_scenes`: its own beat scenes and the recent window, a
    scene whose id collides once normalised left out), c {label (what is
    being asked, `reconcile.LABELS`), records (as `user.j2`'s), signal_text}.
    Every key is always passed; a blank one renders nothing. -#}
{% if now -%}
Campaign date: {{ now }}
{% endif -%}
{% if chronicle -%}
Recent scenes:
{% for s in chronicle -%}
- {{ s.id }} — {{ s.one_line }}
{% endfor -%}
{% endif -%}
{% if now or chronicle %}
{% endif -%}
Candidate — {{ c.label }}
{%- for r in c.records %}
{{ r.letter }}{% if r.type %} ({{ r.type }}){% endif %}: {{ r.line }}
{%- for b in r.beats %}
  {% if b.scene %}[{{ b.scene }}] {% endif %}{{ b.text }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- if r.pressure %}
  pressure: {{ r.pressure }}
{%- endif %}
{%- if r.links %}
  links: {{ r.links | join("; ") }}
{%- endif %}
{%- if r.actors %}
  people: {{ r.actors | join(", ") }}
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- if c.signal_text %}
signals: {{ c.signal_text }}
{%- endif %}
